Hi nimble developers,  I have recently upgraded nimble to version 0.13.0, which includes the new structures for handling posterior predictive nodes (PPN).  For my particular model, including a PPN seems to cause sampling issues, especially for the slice sampler on any discrete nodes in the model (i.e. "slice sampler reached maximum number of contractions...").  However, when I remove the PPN from the model, the model samples just fine.   This occurs whether I provide initial values for the PPN or not.   The other parts of the model are fully initialised.

It seems like a bug but it could be that I am doing something wrong.   I have attached a copy of the model and data so the issue can be reproduced.  The model code has the PPN commented out so uncomment to reproduce the issue.

Happy to provide more context if needed.  I am using R 4.2.2 on Win10.

thanks and regards
Dave

